AgentHawk CLI is defensive, dual-use security software.

It exposes local commands that inspect npm dependency metadata, repository dependency manifests, and Git dependency diffs, then applies deterministic policy before a dependency is admitted. Its intended use is to help developers and coding agents identify risk signals and require explicit review.

The package does not install or execute inspected package code, exploit systems, collect credentials, or claim that a dependency is benign. Security findings remain limited by the enabled evidence sources and policy.
